# The verifier sd:1107 says was missing. `backup-verify-monthly` was named in
# that row as not loaded; it was never defined either, in this folder or
# anywhere else, so the absence of every off-machine backup went unreported
# until it was discovered by losing work.
#
# This does not check that files exist. It copies the newest sd-db snapshot
# directory off the share and runs sd_db's whole `restore` verb against a
# throwaway home -- nothing writes to the share, nothing touches the live
# store -- then compares the counts against the manifest and re-hashes every
# companion file the manifest names. It runs the real verb rather than a
# selection of its checks, because the database validator alone accepts a
# snapshot whose runner journal restore refuses, and a check that passes what
# restore would refuse is this row's failure one layer down.
#
# The snapshot is all it checks. It also sampled the repos mirror on the NAS
# until 2026-09-23, when that mirror moved to the local USB disk under the
# repos-mirror job and the NAS copy was retired.
#
# The interpreter is the one sd-db.sh picks first, because the validator has
# to be importable; SD_DB_PYTHON overrides it the same way.
#
# An unmounted share exits 1 here, which is the whole point: a quiet pass on a
# missing destination is the failure this row was opened for.
#
# 06:00 is well after sd-db-backup's 02:10 run has written the snapshot to
# the USB disk and then carried it to the NAS.
JOB_SCHEDULE="0 6 * * *"
JOB_COMMAND="\"${SD_DB_PYTHON:-$HOME/repos/platypeeps/sd-workflow/.venv/bin/python}\" \"$ROOT/../local-mirror-sync/offsite-verify.py\""
